{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427380-new-era-lore-headcanons","id":1427380,"title":"New Era Lore & Headcanons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-05T10:01:35-08:00","id":1427380,"title":"New Era Lore & Headcanons","content":"So vampire has always enjoyed a wealth of attention attached to it as the main world of darkness flagship game line, but for those of us who enjoy using canon materials as inspiration for our home games, it\u2019s impossible not to note that after 2005 and until the release of V20 and V5 (and even then comparatively) there\u2019s a slight drought of material, at least relatively, so in the spirit of crowd sourcing I extend questions to y\u2019all.<br /> <br /> How do y\u2019all think vampires have/would have reacted to the past two decades? Whether political, cultural, or technological developments; what do you think might have happened or would be interesting if it had happened? What do you think might have happened to various sects, clans, factions, or even individual vampires?<br /> <br /> Now to head this off at the pass - I\u2019m interested in V20 and V5 and everything in between. I\u2019m happy to see people post ideas which could fit within either paradigms or neither. All I ask is that this not become a pissing match in either direction - every perspective is valid so long as it is meaningful to the people who subscribe to it and facilitates their enjoyment of the setting.<br /> <br /> With that having been said, to sum up, my intention as OP is for this thread to basically serve as a resource for ideas, inspiration, headcanons, and potential plot hooks to illustrate the setting of the World of Darkness in the era following the end of the revised gameline era.<br /> <br /> All that said, I hope folks enjoy this thread and it can provide both inspiration and a creative outlet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T10:32:56-08:00","id":1427383,"title":"","content":"To get it started with some ideas...<br /> <br /> \u2022The Gangrel Exodus<br /> A large segment of clan Gangrel left the Camarilla after the departure of Xaviar. While certainly not all left and in fact many remain amongst every sect, the Gangrel always had a cultural bias towards independence. They have always been a clan of survivors and their culture has often seen them eschew the society of their cousins of the blood.<br /> <br /> Now the Gangrel are spread across the world and independent domains stripe the wilderness. Scandinavia and the American Heartland have both proven strong examples. In Scandinavia, alongside the rise of the Anarchs and the Valkyrie faction, the Gangrel happily establish domains across the wilderness and hinterlands of Northern Europe. Similar practices follow in the Midwest and Southwest where Gangrel have become well known to stalk the back countries and wildernesses which others must now avoid. While the accounts of new Viking &amp; Native American cultures are somewhat exaggerated, the old ways have always been popular amongst the outlanders. The reports of Gangrel raiders however are fairly accurate and many suburban and urban domains have been forced out of necessity to come to agreements with independent domains of Gangrel to keep them from wanton poaching and raiding of resources. In many ways, despite the shock of many ancillae, elders find this to be actually a return to the norm for much of Clan Gangrel.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Web<br /> Though the elders may not have liked it, the democratization of the internet and the digital revolution made vampires online impossible to avoid. Many neonates and almost fledgelings were born and embraced into a digital world and it\u2019s become so expansive that it\u2019s more suspicious now to not be online somewhat then to be online if you\u2019re a western youth. While the elders and ancillae tried to forbid the use of the internet this was impossible to enforce and seeing any attempts as ceding cyberspace to the Anarchs the other sects were forced to adapt. Now as ScreckNET (the public version at least, the Nosferatu aren\u2019t giving up the moderator powers or their own layers of operation) spreads across the neonates like wildfire alongside techno-mystical applications like FangBook and the BloodSpot, though the Camarilla and Sabbat elders watch it warily, almost every neonate (the majority of kindred) are online to some degree.<br /> <br /> This has naturally been a boon and a curse. Fears of Masquerade Breaches over YouTube were realized yet the impact was made less disastrous due to the sheer flood of misinformation which the internet allowed for. While Nosfetatu, Alastors, and Templars scour the internet for genuine masquerade breaches they come across more good-looking fakes done with special effects then they do breaches themself. However this being the case is no reason to get lazy, as young fledgelings are often warned and yet sometimes seem to struggle to comprehend.<br /> <br /> The internet has made its own cultures and instant communication has allowed for vampiric culture to develop even more mystery and rumor while somehow being more informed. Legends, gossip, and stories fly rapidly with accounts of the jyhad stretching the globe. Ventrue and Toreador flaunt their skills to the praise of hundreds world-over or find themselves global mockeries after failures. Brujah are able to whip one another into even greater frenzies in digital echo chambers and chat room rants. The Malkavians are a wealth of information and misformation who\u2019ve made the internet a second home (and none are better at memes). The Nosferatu walk through the internet as social masters as they can be nowhere else; in the age where information is king they are emperors.<br /> <br /> While the Camarilla and Sabbat as institutions struggle to keep up with neonates tutoring ancillae who discourse with elders (as well as legions of dedicated ghouls and thralls operating and monitoring) the internet remains an existential terror for many ancilllae and most elders. While they have struggled to gain more prominence and presence, and corporate &amp; government data mining has been something of a relief to them, they remain in dread because of one undeniable truth. The internet is the domain of the Anarchs and the young - and the young shall ever rise up against their elders...<br /> <br /> \u2022Globalization <br /> Vampiric domains are historically isolated fiefs and throughout the majority clan cultures have been what connect kindred across geographic lines. Sects and Proto-Sects may have united disparate domains but always due to proximity and common interest. Given the secretive and careful nature of kindred, while stories of global struggle were ever popular, most kindred knew nothing of their kin a few day\u2019s travel away much less across continents and even the globe.<br /> <br /> This is no longer the case. Rapid travel allows one to traverse the globe in a matter of hours. Instant communication allows for messages to travel in seconds. The kindred, as antiquated as they are, could not deprive themselves of such an obvious resource. While Anarchs and youths may have realized the possibilities first, elders and the older sects had more resources with which to exploit those possibilities.<br /> <br /> So now, though always through proxy, clans and sects can communicate in instant. An elder raises a finger, a ghoul transcribes a message, and in minutes the elder\u2019s descendants from New York to Hong Kong receive their instructions. Sects are able to mobilize and communicate more effectively then ever before, even through the intricate matrix of codes and proxies which elders demand for a sense of security. When a Camarilla city in Canada falls to a Sabbat siege; the Camarilla leadership in Europe can react to the news in moments and begin ordering misinformation and spin doctoring, while Anarchs in the US can spread the news across the Movement in instants, and Sabbat as far as Argentina can celebrate a victory for the Sword of Caine.<br /> <br /> What more this era of travel and communication has made it inevitable that contact between the sects of the west and other sects grow. Bloodlines, independents, and groups such as the Laibon and the Vampiric Courts of Asia inevitability become slowly more known and while secrecy and difficulties making contact remain, with every year the world gets smaller and smaller...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T11:38:20-08:00","id":1427392,"title":"","content":"-There is way too much bullshit on the internet, and Ventrue, Toreador, Tremere and Lasombra have financed multiple propaganda machine organizations with the sole purpose of putting more bullshit onto the internet. The Tremere have even invented spells for putting bullshit on the internet. <br /> <br /> -I like RotB. But after some research I'm getting the idea that 'chaos magic' is dying, but also there's a ton of potential magical practices invented in the last century and a half and I think through communication the Anarchs are going to get better at it. I like the idea that thaumaturgy is becoming more available, and I think the second level ritual that disables machines is becoming a hot item. I'd imagine there's more pressure on the Tremere to not-ash everything that can thaumaturge, an even some token 'we'll let them learn a little bit' (&quot;I mean, if we teach em, we can control their rate of growth and discourage other practices from developing to meet demand!&quot;) As Thaumaturgy is a hard thing to learn and dependent on teachers, the Tremere aren't going to heavily scrutinise everyone who learns the first or second level. <br /> <br /> -Vicissitude and the right for a vampire to change their immutable body's a hot topic, with more neonates taking a progressive interest, and others getting more reactionary. But since near-all elders take the reactionary stance, a lot of neonates are getting stomped for it. <br /> <br /> -Schismatic assamites are getting a lot of shtick for stuff loyalists are doing. But also Schismatic assamites don't actually agree with eachother on a lot of things. Some Schismatics left because Ur-Shulgi's a nutter. Others left because Ur-Shulgi was persecuting the religious. The thing is; A lot of schismatics still don't like the religious among them, and different religious groups don't like eachother. Modern Islam is completely hostile to the practice of Assamite Sorcery while other modern faiths don't fare much better, and a lot of Assamites just find the twisted ways that vampires adhere to religion while breaking all of it's tenants abhorrent and hypocritical, especially since Assamites are supposed to be above the petty squablings of other &quot;kindred&quot;. Some of the Schismatics are religious extremists worse than even the Loyalists on the path of blood. The Schismatics are rife with schism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T14:31:06-08:00","id":1427402,"title":"","content":"-The Followers of Set become increasingly tied to the Old World and do not maintain much oversight to the New World these nights. The reasons for such are many from the uptick of instability, concurrent war, increasing poverty; the works. Though it doesn't tie-up the Followers of Set in the way of you think its bad, on the contrary with all the madness about the Middle-East their cults continue and influences continue to grow at unprecedented heights. However as with the balance of all things, the Setites as mentioned before lose significant influences as the Setites in the New World begin to form their own identities and protocols. Above all these newly parceling sub-factions arise the &quot;Ministry of Set&quot; or the &quot;Ministry&quot;. <br /> <br /> This exclave sub-faction quickly becomes the greatest of the New World Setite cult-cells due to the sheer fact they emulate the styles and techniques of the major North American Televangelists with great gusto. As in the farthest of East in the Old World; in the farthest of the West from the bayous of the American south or the urban sprawls of the American north-east the &quot;Minister&quot; grows in number and influence, slowly, but surely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T17:21:01-08:00","id":1427504,"title":"","content":"The Kevin Jackson one is gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T17:30:50-08:00","id":1427505,"title":"","content":"<br /> Rather than do a bunch of important GIANT CLAN AND POLITICS changes, I'm going to do a bunch of small inconsequential character details and hope people enjoy those for what they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Chicago by Night 5E</b><br /> <br /> * Kevin Jackson shaves his head every night due to the embarrassing &quot;Kid and Play&quot; $ sign haircut he's permanently stuck with for the rest of his life. The Tremere are actively trying to get hold of these hair samples.<br /> <br /> * Damien is genuinely surprised that his fellow Anarchs are now MORE committed to the cause than they ever were during the Camarilla days and some are actually willing to die for it. A lot of his old friends don't believe his defection while new ones think he's a monster.<br /> <br /> * Baby Chorus sounds a lot like AC/DC due to the fact that it's a lot harder rock sound than Goth nightclub. That's Kathy Glenn's influence. Their most famous song is one that AC/DC covered in, &quot;If you want Blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Alan Sovereign has an intimate knowlege of hip hop, R&amp;B, and gangsta rap. It's not part of any weird plot, it's just he developed a fondness for it.<br /> <br /> * Horatio Ballard feeding on the children of his family was actually a slander created by Capone.<br /> <br /> * One of the things that Son blackmailed Ballard into doing was being a independent wrestler called the Human Blob. Oddly, he actually enjoyed this and ocassionally still does weekend matches under a mask. He even hired El Diablo Verde to help train him.<br /> <br /> * Bobby Weatherbottom is the founder of the Red Question and the business he wiped out the fortune of was Ballard.<br /> <br /> * Bobby is considering kidnapping Thin Bloods to start feeding on in place of his girlfriend. They're the only viable alternative other than torpor. He's negotiating VERY carefully with Bronwyn.<br /> <br /> * Ballard is actually flat broke. He uses Dominate and Presence to live with his richer family members. It'll take decades to get back his original fortune and it hasn't helped Bobby has continually screwed him over.<br /> <br /> * All of the Primogen and Nosferatu actually know that Khalid is Cedrick Calhoun. They just assume this is him fooling everyone else and are getting a bit annoyed he hasn't dispensed with the pretense yet.<br /> <br /> * Cedrick Calhoun's racist &quot;Middle Eastern Wise Man&quot; interpretation of Khalid HAS fooled Kevin Jackson completely.<br /> <br /> * Joseph Peterson is now working for the RED Network and was involved with the Trump campaign. He's thorougly aligned with Pentex now and does frequent commentary for the new.<br /> <br /> * Nerissa Blackwater is just a 5th Generation Brujah and her claims of mysteriousness are largely that, claims.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chicago Folio</b><br /> <br /> * Kevin Jackson exiled the Wolf Pack because he hates the idea of Archons having authority over him. He also distrusts Gangrel due to their leaving the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> * Prince Decker has made <i>numerous</i> offers to the Wolf Pack to join him in Milwaukee and they're honestly not sure why they haven't taken him up on it yet.<br /> <br /> * Al Capone's quest for enlightenment has led him to the Church of Caine. He's still not entirely certain he wants to leave behind his Catholicism but the local branch is close enough that he gets by it.<br /> <br /> * Gabrielle Twitch streams <i>Revenant: The Ravishing</i> games with Arthur Caldwell and Bobby Weatherbottom plus multiple other vampires. It is a huge Masquerade breach.<br /> <br /> * Lianne Miller got her name from X-Factor comics.<br /> <br /> <b>Let the Streets Run Red</b><br /> <br /> * Walter Nash also goes by &quot;Sir&quot; in conversations despite never being to England in his life.<br /> <br /> * Walter Nash used to be put in charge of Chicago while Lodin was visiting London. This was not because he trusted Nash but because he figured Nash would irritate everyone so much that they would be delighted when he returned (and he was right). This is why Nash has considered himself the Prince of Chicago sometimes.<br /> <br /> * The Sleeping God may be a Earthbound or Bane imprisoned by the Uktena. It might also be nothing.<br /> <br /> * Honor is a lesbian and her sire is quite irritated with that discovery since he fell in &quot;love&quot; with her from a far. Decker is many things but not a rapist so he's attempting to adjust his feelings accordingly.<br /> <br /> * The Ministry teachers in Indianapolis are actually REALLY BAD at their job. Their attempts to merge Christian fundamentalism and Setite logic fail for everyone as they don't know the Path of Heaven or other ways. As such, they're just driving their subjects to the Beast.<br /> <br /> * Evelyn Stephens is actually Blood Bound to Juggler but he did a much better job of managing it.<br /> <br /> * Gregory Stephens and Sullivan Dane took out Lucian despite the fact he was Beckoned.<br /> <br /> * &quot;Charlie&quot; is not a renamed Michael but Michael's childe who was actually a child when Embraced. Charlie diablerized Michael and was mentored by Son.<br /> <br /> * Arthur doesn't have a split personality but is a sleeper agent for Maxwell among the Anarchs. Ironically, Maxwell couldn't prepare for the fact that Arthur has the True Love merit to Allicia.<br /> <br /> * Allicia thinks that Arthur is Blood Bound to her but his True Love merit means it didn't take. Ironically, she doesn't realize his feelings are sincere. It's also why she's the one exception to his Obsession (Vengeance) Derangement.<br /> <br /> * Allicia, rather than do Jazz, actually does symphonic metal and sounds a lot like Lzzy Hale. This is due to a chance meeting with them in Chicago and her falling for Lzzy's sound.<br /> <br /> * Daughters of Darkness is based on her and Evelyn's adventures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3XQ1FB3Rz0g\" data-code=\"3XQ1FB3Rz0g\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3XQ1FB3Rz0g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> * Eric Sharpe is addicted to Fringe and Bosch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 12-09-2020, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T18:00:49-08:00","id":1427506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427380-new-era-lore-headcanons?p=1427504#post1427504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kevin Jackson one is gold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have the fact that Kevin Jackson is a HUGE Johnny Cash and old school country fan but he can't listen to that in the presence of his men.<br /> <br /> It gets funnier when Sovereign tries to chat him up about Jay Z.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T22:41:47-08:00","id":1427811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427380-new-era-lore-headcanons?p=1427392#post1427392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Vicissitude and the right for a vampire to change their immutable body's a hot topic, with more neonates taking a progressive interest, and others getting more reactionary. But since near-all elders take the reactionary stance, a lot of neonates are getting stomped for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I have some V20 (and technically V5 if I ever get a chance to play it and depending on what they do with the Tzimisce in the upcoming V5 Companion) concepts similar to that. The Anarch Tzimisce (seriously why did it take until V20 for the Tzimisce to have a presence in a Sect besides the Sabbat) had long used their powers as a means of espionage (assuming the form of a Cam/Sabbat vampire) or hiding from their foes in plain sight but in more recent nights there's been a growing movement akin to that among vampires. Some are neonates that were Trans in life but hadn't transitioned while they were alive seeking the chance to have a body they're comfortable with. Others are just looking for a thrill and even some jaded elder Cam Torries have quietly approached Anarch Tzimisce about experiencing a night in a different face or gender.<br /> <br /> In V5, between what happened to them in BJD and the Beckoning/Gehenna Crusade, led Vykos leading a chunk of a Sabbat Tzimisce to the Anarchs, bolstering their existing Anarch cousins. As for Tzimisce and the Beckoning, some have called but most haven't, leading to most in the Clan thinking they're immune because [Tzimisce] is dead. What only a few know is that indeed some have been Beckoned but not all of them have been Elders and not all of them headed for the Middle East. Vykos is one such individual has discovered this and has come to fear with everything that's happened that the Sabbat had long been or is currently being co-opted by the Elders just as the Camarilla had been, their warriors going off on their crusade as nothing more than pawns in the Elders' games. After what he witnessed with Mary the Black and Michael, what he experienced with the Dracon, old assumptions on the powers of the Elders have shattered. The Anarchs may possibly be the only group that hasn't really had the Elders' tendrils in.<br /> <br /> And on a more personal level, Vykos is still working through who they are without the Dracon within their body and influencing them.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Anarchs view this Sabbat defection as a mixed bag. On the one hand, they're not crazy about a bunch of Sabbat joining their ranks but at the same time, they can't really afford to just turn them away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T00:48:48-08:00","id":1427823,"title":"","content":"<b>More Character Bits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Brujah</b><br /> <br /> * Gengis voted for Trump. He claims he voted for Bernie. The fact he's a registered voter at all is a surprising fact.<br /> <br /> * Critias' wise elder statesman persona for the past 3000 years was basiclaly Menele possessing him. His actual personality is a toadying asshole coward and rampant misogynist. A lot of people are wondering if he's suffering a midlife crisis or something given his dramatic change in personality.<br /> <br /> * Theo Bell absolutely loves the Blade movies. He'd never admit it, though. He copied a huge chunk of Snipes' style.<br /> <br /> <b>Caitiff</b><br /> <br /> * Gordon Keaton was the basis for &quot;American Psycho&quot; as he was the Trump supporting college roommate of Bret Easton Ellis who inspired him. Gordon eventually saw the movie and unironically thought it was a moving story about one man's inner pain.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b><br /> <br /> * Sierra Burrace was a terrible Sabbat and only the Vinculum kept her from being killed. Studying hard, making mortal resources, and being cheerful about your job were just never working out for her.<br /> <br /> * Talley has an uncanny resemblance to Aiden Gillan. Talley is prone to frenzy due to the idea of looking like an Irishman (he sounds like one too but he has no idea how that happened).<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian</b><br /> <br /> * Arthur Caldwell prefers to feeds on Neo-Nazis, Alt-Right trolls, and Qanon followers. He's had very little difficulty hunting these past few years.<br /> <br /> <b>Ministry</b><br /> <br /> * Marcel's drug, sex, and Egyptian wallpaper cult is one of the most stereotypical Followers of Set ones you could ever meet. So much so that most Followers of Set assumed he was kidding when they visited and he shows up in full Pharoah garb. It's not him being ignorant, he's just very very tacky in his tastes.<br /> <br /> * Marcel only became a member of the Ministry because no one in the Church of Set wanted him. Hesha actually just invited him in because of a weird sense of pity.<br /> <br /> * He doesn't get why they call can't just get along, smoke some ganja, and worship Set, ya know?<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu</b><br /> <br /> * Adze is leading a Blood Cult of Caitiff larger and more organized than all of the Anarchs in Chicago. He's effectively the &quot;true&quot; Baron of the Anarchs in the city but was smart enough to just tell his followers to stay out of the other Kindred's hotspots and way for decades.<br /> <br /> * Nathaniel Borduff made several million dollars last year when his church merged to become an online megachurch. This confuses him on several levels and has actually distracted him from his vampire hunting mission.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador</b><br /> <br /> * Brett Stryker unironically listens to &quot;I'm Too Sexy&quot; and other glam male ballads constantly. Anyone who spends any time with him will learn to hate these songs beyond recompense.<br /> <br /> * Tamoszius has attempted on no less than three occassions to Embrace Lindsay Sterling. Kathy Glen has stopped him because he hasn't the permission of the Prince and also out of a weird sense of jealousy.<br /> <br /> * Damien and Garwood didn't realize Kathy was Indian American for decades until she started wearing a sari and cleaning her hair. Kathy finds this immensely racist.<br /> <br /> * Helena has 2 million followers on her Instagram account. Most people assume she's photoshopped herself. It's not so much a Masquerade breach as a blindingly dumb thing to do. The Second Inquisition have ignored her because no Kindred could be that stupid.<br /> <br /> * Helena is on the final leg to wightdom due to all the diablerie she's doing. On the other hand, her sheer willpower means that it will be a sudden snapping of her brain from conscious to mindless Godzilla-like killer.<br /> <br /> * On Allicia's hypothetical lore sheet, she has franchised the Torch strip clubs and they've made her a very wealthy woman. She has no desire for this to become public knowledge among Kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b><br /> <br /> * Erichtho doesn't want to join House Carna because she fully believes that Carna is a serial killing psychopath just pretending to be a New Age spiritual leader in order to lure impressionable Tremere under her wing.<br /> <br /> * Carna is actually a serial killing psychopath just pretending to be a New Age spiritual leader in order to lure impressionable Tremere under her wing. Oh and she thinks Erichtho is a stuck up ****.<br /> <br /> * Sun Che is not actually possessed. She's just a murderous psychopath with a split personality.<br /> <br /> * Garwood Marshall has been trying to contact the band as a wraith for decades. The Lasombra have finally allowed him to do so. His message from beyond the grave? &quot;Being dead sucks. Also, we need to bring back the saxaphone to hard rock.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue</b><br /> <br /> * Olaf could be cured of his condition by Helena or Eletria's ancient blood. He could also be healed by powerful dialberie. None of which anyone wants to give him access to.<br /> <br /> * Olaf's condition is not due to the Sabbat or Lupines but due to him falling into the hands of Son for decades.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535